<title>USA: Computer Sciences team seeks big IRS pact.</title>
<headline>Computer Sciences team seeks big IRS pact.</headline>
<dateline>EL SEGUNDO, Calif. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Computer Sciences Corp said it has teamed up with International Business Machines Corp, Northrop Grumman Corp, SAIC of France and Unisys Corp to bid for a $3 billion 15-year contract to streamline the tax administration system at the Internal Revenue Service.</p>
<p>Computer Sciences said it would be the prime contractor if the group were awarded the contract, which is expected to be announced in the third or fourth quarter of 1998.</p>
<p>Another group, headed by Lockheed Martin Corp, has announced its plans to bid for the contract as well, Computer Sciences spokesman Pay Ways said.</p>
</text>
